<title>RUSSIA: Russian 6-mth T-bill yield falls to 54.06 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 6-mth T-bill yield falls to 54.06 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annualised yield on an issue of six-month GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 54.06 percent at an auction on Wednesday from 58.46 percent at the previous auction of six-month paper on October 30, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Full details of the issue:</p>
<p>				    Nov 6		   Oct 30</p>
<p>    Series number	     22057		   22056</p>
<p>    Issue volume		8.00 trln rbls	9.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million rbls	 1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	   11.49 trln	    10.07 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	    7.99 trln	     6.92 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		    5.95 trln	     5.71 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	    74.51 pct	     82.44 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price  74.36 pct	     82.20 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	    54.06 pct	     58.46 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield 54.48 pct	     59.43 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 231 days	     133 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     June 25, 1997	March 12, 1997</p>
<p>On November 6 the finance ministry will auction off 2.50 trillion roubles of a new tranche of the OFZ two-year bonds maturing in March 1998 (series 24007).</p>
<p>It will also repay about 5.97 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of six-month T-bills (series 23032) and pay about 1.02 trillion roubles in interest on the two-year government bond maturing in February 1998 (series 24006).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
